   "evidence": "The sibling API in the same family keeps bodies hidden and uses the parenthesised form: `Overlattice/Basic.lean:92` `def discriminantSubgroup` and `:126` `def intermediateCarrierOfDiscriminantSubgroup` carry no `@[expose]`, and their reduction lemmas at `:100` and `:137` are proved `(rfl)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Index.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[expose]` from both definitions; the public contract is `relIndex_def`, `index_def` and `relIndex_eq_natCard_quotient`. Also state the definitional lemmas as `:= (rfl)` (lines 109, 114, 138) so downstream proofs cannot bake in the defeq.",
   "issue": "`relIndex` (line 97-99) and `index` (line 103-105) are marked `@[expose]`, making the `AddSubgroup.relIndex` implementation part of the public contract. Both are `noncomputable`, nothing downstream consumes them, and every in-module `rfl` proof (`relIndex_def`, `index_def`, `relIndex_bot_left`) works without exposure since bodies are visible in their defining module.",
   "line": "97"
  }
 ],
